efforts to modernize state aid policy  top the agenda when ministers  responsible for improving the European  Union's competitiveness meet in Brussels  in public deliberations the ministers  are expected to reach a political  agreement on the upgrade as the EU seeks  to focus on the most efficient and  ferris state aid airports and airlines  have routinely been involved in state  aid cases amid concerns about unfair  competition the idea is to ensure that  state funding helps address real market  failures promotes a competitive single  market and provides the best outcome for  the lowest price particularly in times  of recession if all goes according to  plan the reform could be completed by  the end of the year the European  Parliament must endorse the package for  it to enter into force also in open  forum the ministers will discuss  copyright rules in the EU and the  protection of authors and artists to  help foster creativity the plan is to  brainstorm ways to set up a more modern  framework for considering copyright laws  in the digital age and share views on  the e use fragmented markets in this  area the issue of private copying and  imposing levies in the EU has been tough  to resolve copyright levies vary widely  from country to country they can become  a lucrative source of income for rights  holders but can also create obstacles to  the free movement of goods and services  Europe's future research programme  horizon 2020 is also on the agenda The  ministers will assess progress made in  negotiations with the European  Parliament using their inputs the Irish  presidency hopes to reach an early  agreement on the seven-year programme  research ministers will also debate  joint programming which sets out ways to  best tackle the many challenges facing  society by better use of resources 10  such programs have been launched since  2009 on challenges like brain disorders  climate change and Urban Development
 

